# Matsuoka et al. (2018, ApJ 869, 150), Table 4 ("Binned luminosity function"), standard rows; checked against arXiv:1811.01963v1
# Sample: combined SDSS + CFHQS + SHELLQs complete quasar samples (one binned LF derived from all three)
# Redshift: 5.7 <= z <= 6.5 (parametric LF quoted at z = 6.0)
# Magnitude definition: M1450; bin width 0.5 mag except -22.00 (1.0 mag), -27.50 (1.0 mag) and -29.00 (2.0 mag)
# Phi convention: linear Phi in units of 1e-9 cMpc^-3 mag^-1 (table in Gpc^-3 mag^-1); H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7
# Note: These are the paper's standard values, which include the five SHELLQs objects with narrow Lyalpha (FWHM < 500 km/s) and are
#       used for its standard parametric fit. The last two rows of Table 4 ("for reference") exclude those objects:
#       M1450 = -22.75: 14.4 +- 6.4; M1450 = -23.25: 8.5 +- 3.2. They are NOT used here.
# Note: The -22.00 and -29.00 bins contain one quasar each (Phi - Delta = 0).
#
# M1450  Phi  Delta
 -22.000  16.2  16.2
 -22.750  23.0  8.1
 -23.250  10.9  3.6
 -23.750  8.3  2.6
 -24.250  6.6  2.0
 -24.750  7.0  1.7
 -25.250  4.6  1.2
 -25.750  1.33  0.60
 -26.250  0.90  0.32
 -26.750  0.58  0.17
 -27.500  0.242  0.061
 -29.000  0.0079  0.0079
